    <aside class="notes">
        <p>Friday afternoon. You open a small pull request. And the CI is red.</p>
        <p>The failing test has nothing to do with your change. A third-party API did not answer. A timeout, a 503, a rate limit.</p>
        <p>So you click "re-run". It's green. You merge. Like this little dog: "This is fine."</p>
        <p>But it's not fine. When a test fails for no reason, we stop listening to it. And the day it fails for a real reason, nobody looks.</p>
        <p>So, my question today: how do we test code that calls the outside world, without depending on it?</p>
